# Disable runtime PM for WSA881x speaker amps to fix silent boot on Pocket Max.
#
# The Pocket Max wires BOTH amps to one powerdown line (tlmm 127, declared on
# speaker@0,1 and speaker@0,2). gpiolib hands each consumer a gpiolib_shared
# proxy over that single line, and a shared line aggregates its consumers, so one
# amp left in runtime-suspend holds the other in powerdown too. The stuck amp then
# never completes SoundWire enumeration:
#     wsa881x-codec sdw:1:0:0217:2010:00:1: Initialization not complete
#     WSA Playback: ASoC error (-110): at __soc_pcm_open()
# runtime PM latches the device in the error state and the whole card is unusable.
#
# Pinning both amps active from bind keeps the line de-asserted. The Retroid
# boards use the same wsa881x part but give each amp its own powerdown line,
# so they keep runtime PM and the amps power down when idle and in suspend.
# Only the MANGMI boards (Pocket Max, Air Y Pro) share the line.
ACTION=="bind", SUBSYSTEM=="soundwire", KERNEL=="sdw:*:0217:2010:*", PROGRAM="/usr/bin/grep -qs MANGMI /sys/firmware/devicetree/base/model", ATTR{power/control}="on"
